    37	**ABSTRACT**
    38	
    39	
    40	In this experience paper, we share our experience on enhancing
    41	automatic unit test generation to more effectively find Java null
    42	pointer exceptions (NPEs). NPEs are among the most common and
    43	critical errors in Java applications. However, as we demonstrate in
    44	this paper, existing unit test generation tools such as Randoop and
    45	EvoSuite are not sufficiently effective at catching NPEs. Specifically,
    46	their primary strategy of achieving high code coverage does not
    47	necessarily result in triggering diverse NPEs in practice. In this
    48	paper, we detail our observation on the limitations of current stateof-the-art unit testing tools in terms of NPE detection and introduce
    49	a new strategy to improve their effectiveness. Our strategy utilizes
    50	both static and dynamic analyses to guide the test case generator
    51	to focus specifically on scenarios that are likely to trigger NPEs.
    52	We implemented this strategy on top of EvoSuite, and evaluated
    53	our tool, NpeTest, on 108 NPE benchmarks collected from 96 realworld projects. The results show that our NPE-guidance strategy
    54	can increase EvoSuite’s reproduction rate of the NPEs from 56.9%
    55	to 78.9%, a 38.7% improvement. Furthermore, NpeTest successfully
    56	detected 89 previously unknown NPEs from an industry project.
