    68	**1** **INTRODUCTION**
    69	
    70	
    71	Null pointer exceptions (NPEs) are one of the most common and fatal errors in Java applications [ 1 – 6 ]. NPE is a critical software defect
    72	because dereferencing a null pointer always makes the program
    73	crash, causing undefined behavior of the entire system. In addition
    74	to the hazardous impacts of NPEs on software, NPEs frequently
