   102	Therefore, software testing is mandatory to reduce the risk of NPEs
   103	during the software development process.
   104	
   105	
   106	_**Unit Testing.**_ Unit testing has been one of the most widely
   107	used software testing techniques for object-oriented programming
   108	languages such as Java. With well-designed test cases that represent
   109	the usage scenarios of a certain unit to test, unit testing validates
   110	that each unit of the software performs as expected, where a unit is
   111	typically an individual method or object. Due to its characteristics
   112	that enable testing of an individual single unit with diverse usage
   113	scenarios, unit testing helps facilitate software maintainability and
   114	is used to prevent future regressions, which improves overall software quality during the development process. From this perspective,
   115	unit tests are widely utilized to detect software defects. However,
   116	finding bug-triggering unit tests is a complex and time-consuming
   117	task, which becomes more difficult with respect to the size and
   118	complexity of software systems.
   119	
   120	
   121	_**Automatic Unit Test Generation.**_ To reduce the burdens of
   122	
   123	developers on designing unit tests, automatic test case generation
   124	techniques have been proposed with two major approaches: random
   125	testing and search-based software testing. Both methods generate
   126	test cases by automatically synthesizing method call sequences for
   127	the target unit, without assuming existing test drivers.
   128	Random testing is a simple yet effective approach to automatically generating method sequences for object-oriented programs.
   129	It randomly synthesizes a sequence of method calls to generate
   130	test cases. Among various strategies, feedback-directed random
   131	testing has been considered superior to pure random testing, which
   132	is implemented in tools such as Randoop [ 9 ]. Rather than blindly
   133	generating test cases, Randoop leverages the knowledge obtainable through the execution of generated test cases. It runs contract
   134	checkers for each generated object to maintain a pool of valid objects. This feedback-directed approach has become a primary test
   135	generation strategy for programs written in Java and C#.
   136	Search-based software testing (SBST), on the other hand, formulates the test generation as an optimization problem concerning
   137	certain coverage criteria (e.g., branch coverage, exception coverage).
   138	In particular, EvoSuite [ 10 ] is the state-of-the-art SBST tool for
   139	Java, which leverages genetic algorithms (e.g., DynaMOSA [ 11 ]
   140	and MOSA [ 12 ]) to optimize the test suite. It first randomly generates the initial population similar to random testing, and then
