   212	**2** **MOTIVATING EXAMPLE**
   213	
   214	
   215	Figure 1 describes an NPE found in Qpid Proton-J project [1] . The
   216	root cause of this NPE is the null literal assigned to the variable amqpType in the deduceTypeFromClass method (line 4, Figure
   217	1b), which is returned without refinement. The NPE is thrown at
   218	line 8 in Figure 1a, when dereferencing the return value of the
   219	getType method (line 7, Figure 1a)—which internally calls the
   220	deduceTypeFromClass method shown in Figure 1b and returns
   221	the result directly.
   222	However, the conditions under which the variable amqpType is
   223	not refined during the execution are not trivial. The type of the
   224	first argument should be set properly, which is determined by the
   225	argument of the calculateSize method in Figure 1a. For example,
   226	as shown in Figure 1b, if the type of the first argument when calling
   227	deduceTypeFromClass is an array type, it passes the true branch
   228	at line 5 and amqpType will be redefined, which never triggers NPE.
   229	Also, considering that this method is called in the while loop (line
   230	4, Figure 1a), the input map of the calculateSize method should
   231	contain at least one element.
   232	
   233	Figure 1c is an NPE-triggering test case written by developers,
   234	which leads to NPE whose stack trace is in Figure 1d. By adding
   235	the element in the mapping variable map at line 5, this test case
   236	can enter inside the while loop, which satisfies the first step to
   237	trigger the NPE. Additionally, the instantiation of Map<Integer,
   238	Object> causes the Object type (i.e., Class<Object> ) to be passed
   239	to the first parameter of the deduceTypeFromClass method. This
   240	parameter bypasses the condition at line 5 in Figure 1b as its type is
   241	not an array type, leading deduceTypeFromClass to return null,
   242	which triggers an NPE in Figure 1a.
   243	In order to generate such test cases triggering the NPE, unit test
   244	generation tools must focus on mutating various types for generic
   245	type parameters of Map and find an appropriate one that bypasses
   246	the branch conditions in deduceTypeFromClass not to refine the
