   382	**3** **APPROACH**
   383	
   384	
   385	In this section, we present our approach to guide unit test generators
   386	for better NPE detection. NpeTest consists of two components: (1)
   387	**static analysis** which identifies NPE-prone regions and performs
   388	dependency analysis to track the statement of test case relevant
   389	to NPE-prone regions, and (2) **dynamic analysis** which gathers
   390	runtime information to adaptively update the guidance.
   391	
   392	
   393	**3.1** **Search-Based Software Testing**
   394	
   395	
   396	Algorithm 1 shows the simplified test case generation process
   397	of EvoSuite, a search-based software testing (SBST) tool, which
   398	NpeTest relies on. Initially, the algorithm identifies the coverage
   399	goals _covGoals_ (Line 1), which serve as objectives to guide the
   400	test case generations. It also builds an initial parent population by
   401	randomly generating _𝑁_ test cases (Line 2). The algorithm then generates offspring population from the parent population by randomly
   402	applying various mutation operators such as statement crossover,
   403	insertion, deletion, and change (Line 4). Subsequently, it evaluates
   404	all test cases within both parent and offspring populations by computing their fitness values with respect to each of _covGoals_ . The
   405	promising _TCs_ are selected as the next _parentTCs_, for further test
   406	case exploration (Line 5). In addition, the algorithm can dynamically update _covGoals_ to guide test case generations toward more
   407	promising code regions, thereby achieving more _covGoals_ (Line 6).
   408	Once the given time-budget expires (Line 7), the algorithm returns
   409	the set of test cases, each of which covers at least one coverage goal,
   410	as the final solution (Lines 8–9).
   411	
   412	
   413	_**Workflow of**_ _**NpeTest**_ _**.**_ Algorithm 2 outlines the workflow of
   414	our approach, NpeTest, which builds upon EvoSuite (Algorithm 1).
