     1	# NPETest
     2	This repository contains the source codes for NPETest and other resources inclulding experimental data 
     3	to support the paper "Effective Unit Test Generation for Java Null Pointer Exceptions".
     4	
     5	[paper](./ase2024-paper796.pdf): The accepted version 
     6	
     7	## Requirements
     8	See [REQUIREMENTS.md](./REQUIREMENTS.md).
     9	
    10	## Installation
    11	See [INSTALL.md](./INSTALL.md).
    12	
    13	If you want to perform a small experiment we provide, you can skip the installation step. 
    14	
    15	## Benchmarks
    16	The directory [benchmarks](./benchmarks) contains all benchmarks.
    17	We conducted all experiments in docker system, and we provide the Dockerfile for each benchmark.
    18	* [metadata](./benchmarks/metadata) : contains the known npe information of each benchmark
    19	
    20	The directories below are generated by using script files. For more details, please refer [README](./benchmarks/README.md).
    21	* [dockers](./benchmarks/dockers) : contains Dockerfile files for each benchmark 
    22	* [subject_gits](https://drive.google.com/file/d/11I7m6zamJA5UlWmFlChP6eA76DGozBMb/view?usp=sharing): contains the buggy version of each benchmark.
    23	You can download subject_gits.tar.gz file from the following [link](https://drive.google.com/file/d/11I7m6zamJA5UlWmFlChP6eA76DGozBMb/view?usp=sharing) or [Zenodo](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13738493).
    24	  
    25	## Raw Data for tables in the paper.
    26	* [rq1_result](./rq1_result.xlsx) : contains the result tables for rq1
    27	* [rq2_result](./rq2_result) : contains the result tables for rq2
    28	
    29	For the raw data, we provide additional google drive links for downloading all datas. 
    30	(The data contains all test cases generated by the tools used in our evaluation; hence the size of the data is too large to upload on github.)
    31	
    32	* [NPETest](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oToD6Ecmq8vyDikLEQRqVIJYOkU4-tvO/view?usp=sharing): Google drive link for downloading resultso of NPETest for all benchmarks, containing the generated test-cases.
    33	* [EvoSuite](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PKAYyxqsakE2R9706zSuv3-a0sBRzmBr/view?usp=sharing): Google drive link for downloading resultso of EvoSuite with fine-tuned options for all benchmarks, containing the generated test-cases.
    34	* [EvoSuite_Def](https://drive.google.com/file/d/14AJjoDCm-GYPwLrNaM6g0uvzYT9ltHE3/view?usp=sharing): Google drive link for downloading resultso of EvoSuite with default options for all benchmarks, containing the generated test-cases.
    35	* [Randoop_npex](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mevPl4U9vwRtl0b7bdCu6EpgaMXamx6s/view?usp=sharing): Google drive link for downloading Randoop results for NPEX benchmarks, containing the generated test-cases.
    36	* [Randoop_other](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1i7M7gS0gvp2H9z5BX1ntPx3OQf8PnFcf/view?usp=sharing): Google drive link for downloading Randoop results for Bears, BugSwarm, Defects4J, Genesis benchmarks, containing the generated test-cases.
    37	
    38	For Randoop, we only upload the log files for each benchmark listed in tables since including all test cases generated by Randoop is too large (more than 50GB). 
    39	
    40	You can also download all data from [Zenodo](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13738493).
    41	
    42	## Performing small experiments
    43	
    44	We provide an example instruction which conducts a short experiment running NPETest, EvoSuite, and Randoop on 4 benchmark programs with 5 trials during 5 minutes:
    45	**BungeeCord-1303**, **Feign-9c5a**, **Fastjson-650a**, and **Math-70**.
    46	Note that conducting experiments for all benchmarks (Table 3 in our paper) takes at least 675 hours (5 minutes * 108 benchmarks * 25 trials * 3 tools + additional hours for building benchmarks and tools) on a single core. 
    47	Once the setup instruction is successfully done(or using our VM image), you can perform the small experiments with the following command:
    48	
    49	```
    50	./scripts/running_simple.sh
    51	```
    52	
    53	If all processes are completely done, users can eventually see the testing process logs below:
    54	```
    55	...
    56	[INFO] Running EVOSUITE(NPE_CLASS)_34e5[subject=NPEX:Feign-9c5a52d6] (xx/xx-xx:xx:xx)...
    57	[INFO] Running EVOSUITE(NPE_CLASS)_241s[subject=NPEX:Feign-9c5a52d6] (xx/xx-xx:xx:xx)...
    58	[INFO] Running EVOSUITE(NPE_CLASS)_362a[subject=NPEX:Feign-9c5a52d6] (xx/xx-xx:xx:xx)...
    59	[INFO] Running EVOSUITE(NPE_CLASS)_f213[subject=NPEX:Feign-9c5a52d6] (xx/xx-xx:xx:xx)...
    60	[INFO] Running EVOSUITE(NPE_CLASS)_a142[subject=NPEX:Feign-9c5a52d6] (xx/xx-xx:xx:xx)...
    61	
    62	...
    63	```
    64	
    65	When the experiments are done, please enter the following command to obtain the result table and venn-diagram of unique NPEs detected by each tool:
    66	```
    67	./scripts/build_simple_table.sh
    68	```
    69	
    70	
    71	You can see the tables in "result" directory.
    72	
    73	```
    74	cat ./result/simple_result.txt
    75	```
    76	
    77	
    78	
    79	
    80	* Note that the instructions above were performed on our VM image.
    81	* If users want to perform a small experiment on their local machine, download [subject_gits] and follow the first instruction in [README.md](./benchmarks/README.md). Then, follow the instruction for "**Performing small experiment**".
    82	
    83	
    84	## Reproduction of Results in the Paper
    85	
    86	We provide a python script to reproduce the results of Table 3 in the paper.
    87	We expect all commands are executed on `~/Workspace/ase2024` directory.
    88	
    89	### Generating Table with the existing results. 
    90	
    91	As performing all experiments in our paper takes some time (e.g., approximately 700 hours on a single core), 
    92	we provide a script file to reproduce the results of Table 3 in the paper with the experimental results.
    93	
    94	If users are not using VM image we provide, users must download the "**raw data**", [NPETest](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oToD6Ecmq8vyDikLEQRqVIJYOkU4-tvO/view?usp=sharing), [EvoSuite](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PKAYyxqsakE2R9706zSuv3-a0sBRzmBr/view?usp=sharing), [Randoop_npex](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mevPl4U9vwRtl0b7bdCu6EpgaMXamx6s/view?usp=sharing), [Randoop_other](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1i7M7gS0gvp2H9z5BX1ntPx3OQf8PnFcf/view?usp=sharing), for tables mentioned above,
    95	and place it in result directory. 
    96	
    97	For those who are using VM image, they need to download **raw data** for Randoop only.
    98	
    99	More specifically, please follow the commands below.
   100	
   101	```
   102	mkdir npetest ./result/
   103	mkdir evosuite ./result/
   104	mkdir randoop ./result/
   105	
   106	Unzip the zip files and place the result directory in the corresponding directory.
   107	mv npetest_result ./result/npetest/
   108	mv evosuite_opt_result ./result/evosuite/
   109	...
   110	```
   111	
   112	Once all raw data is placed on the appropriate directory, use the following command to get the result table.
   113	
   114	```
   115	./scripts/get_main_results.sh
   116	```
   117	
   118	You can see the tables in "result" directory.
   119	
   120	```
   121	cat ./result/main_result.txt
   122	
   123	NPEX:
   124	Tool                    evosuite  npetest  randoop
   125	Project
   126	Activiti-c45d6c3c(0)       0          24        0
   127	Aries_JPA-97cb979d(0)    100          80        0
   128	Avro-a3e05bee(0)         100         100       100
   129	...
   130	
   131	```
   132	
   133	
   134	### Generating Tables from a scratch
   135	
   136	Assume that the users follow the installation instructions at [INSTALL.md](./INSTALL.md).
   137	
   138	#### Running NPETest on all benchmarks
   139	After all installation is complete, you can run NPETest on all benchmark programs by using the commands below:
   140	
   141	```
   142	bash -c 'yes | JOB=2 TIME_BUDGET=300 \
   143	  NPE_CLASS_ONLY=1 \
   144	  PYTHON=python3 \
   145	  TOOL=npetest \
   146	  REPEAT=25 \
   147	  OUTPUT_DIR="~/ase2024/result/npetest/npetest_test" \
   148	  ./run_experiment.sh
   149	```
   150	This command runs NPETest 25 times on all benchmarks built by [experiment](./experiment) process, with a time budget of 5 minutes for each benchmark.
   151	
   152	You may change the path for <OUTPUT_DIR>, but the name of parent directory must be "npetest" and the name of the last directory also starts with "npetest_".
   153	For example, the command can be changed as below:
   154	
   155	```
   156	bash -c 'yes | JOB=2 TIME_BUDGET=300 \
   157	  NPE_CLASS_ONLY=1 \
   158	  PYTHON=python3 \
   159	  TOOL=npetest \
   160	  REPEAT=25 \
   161	  OUTPUT_DIR="./result/npetest/npetest_mine" \
   162	  ./run_experiment.sh
   163	```
   164	
   165	Once all experiments are done, you can make the "result.csv" file which represents the number of NPEs detected by using the following command:
   166	
   167	```
   168	./scripts/check_log_file.sh ./result/npetest/npetest_test ./result/npetest_test_result.csv
   169	```
   170	Note that the "csv file" must be inside "result" directory.
   171	
   172	
   173	#### Running other tools on all benchmarks
   174	You can run EvoSuite and Randoop with the same command used for NPETest as follows:
   175	
   176	```
   177	bash -c 'yes | JOB=2 TIME_BUDGET=300 \
   178	  NPE_CLASS_ONLY=1 \
   179	  PYTHON=python3 \
   180	  TOOL=evosuite \
   181	  REPEAT=25 \
   182	  OUTPUT_DIR="~/ase2024/result/evosuite/evosuite_test" \
   183	  ./run_experiment.sh
   184	```
   185	
   186	Please remind that you need to generate "result.csv" file for each tool after the experiments are done.
   187	Note that the "csv file" must be inside "result" directory.
   188	
   189	```
   190	./scripts/check_log_file.sh ./result/evosuite/evosuite_test ./result/evosuite_test_result.csv
   191	```
   192	
   193	
   194	#### Generating Table
   195	
   196	After generating "XX_result.csv" files for all tools (NPETest, EvoSuite, and Randoop), you need to merge the csv files into one csv file as follows:
   197	
   198	```
   199	./scripts/merge_csv_files.sh ./result/merged_result.csv
   200	```
   201	Note that all "XX_result.csv" files must be located in "result" directory.
   202	
   203	Then, you can obtain the result table with the following python code.
   204	```
   205	python3 ./scripts/build_table.py ./result/merged_result.csv ./result/final_result.txt
   206	```
   207	This script csollects all the results in the merged csv file and pretty-print the result as a table.
   208	
   209	
   210	
   211	


